Iterate populate/close to a fixed point

Make walk_rule re-entrant: it now traverses the entire rule body on
every call instead of short-circuiting at statements with a recorded
stmt_after, and re-attempts func/pred resolution at every app term and
pred atom so a reference that was unresolvable on the first pass gets
emitted once close has settled enough type information.

Structure::equate, Structure::close and StructureCat::close now report
whether they observed any work, and walk_rule does the same.
build_structures loops walk_rule + close until both report no change in
the same iteration.

Per-AST-site memoisation: RuleStructures gains branch_block_starts,
match_after_scrutinee and match_case_starts so cloned structures for
those sites are reused rather than re-created on each pass. App-term
result els fed through walk_term's semantic_els cache are propagated
into emit_app as the expected result, so re-resolution writes the new
FuncApp against the cached el (with an equate to any pre-existing
entry).
